[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   Step 143: Comet non-gravitational acceleration channel (step_b107).
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   Published NG parameters are used throughout this work only as an
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   exclusion control (the NG-clean subsets).  They are never read as an
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   observable.  Under the boundary-slip picture they should carry the
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   anomaly in a specific way: a proper-time slip absorbed by a
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   pure-gravity fit must leak into whichever free parameter absorbs a
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   timing error, and in the Marsden formulation that parameter is the
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   transverse NG term A2 (the component that changes the fitted orbital
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   period).  The Warsaw catalogue publishes A1/A2/A3 with uncertainties
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   plus the outgassing-peak time shift tau for every comet whose orbit
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   required an NG solution (tableb4, J/A+A/567/A126).
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   This step reads the NG record as a directional channel against the
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   declared cap (theta < 60 deg to the (34,-13) transit axis, taken from
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   the step_b30 per-comet record):
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T1  NG-model incidence: fraction of the Warsaw cohort fitted with an
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   NG orbit (tablea1 Model column), in-cap vs out-cap.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T2  Transverse leakage: signed A2 and significance-weighted A2/e_A2
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   in-cap vs out-cap, plus A2 against cos(theta) over the full cohort.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   The slip is time-domain; A2 is the timing parameter.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T3  Radial/normal controls: the same tests on A1 and A3 -- a genuine
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   boundary signal should load preferentially into the transverse
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   component, not uniformly into all three.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T4  Time-shift channel: the fitted outgassing-peak offset tau in-cap
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   vs out-cap.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T5  Confound audit: NG solutions are preferentially fitted to
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   well-observed, brighter comets -- n_obs and arc-length medians
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   in-cap vs out-cap among NG members, and an n_obs-matched
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   sensitivity bound on the T2 contrast.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T6  Era note: the Warsaw NG record is pre-2011; the channel is
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   registered on the cohort that carries the declared anomaly.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   T7  Independent replication: the same transverse-term cap contrast on
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   the JPL SBDB NG record (model_pars in the full-precision orbit
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   files), pre-2018 and post-2017 cohorts -- a second orbit pipeline
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   with no Warsaw input.
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   Outputs: results/step_b107_comet_ng_channel.json/.csv and
[2026-09-21 15:17:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 143]   results/figures/supplementary/step_b107_comet_ng_channel.png.
